WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.840
Two monkeyflowers can be crossed by hand to give hybrid seed.

2
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.180
One has pink flowers, visited mostly by bumblebees.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.540
The other has red flowers, visited mostly by hummingbirds.

4
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:25.700
Yet the barriers measured between them were estimated to block, on average, 99.87% of gene flow.

5
00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:27.880
What holds them apart?

6
00:00:28.833 --> 00:00:34.573
A reproductive barrier is anything that reduces gene flow between populations.

7
00:00:35.553 --> 00:00:37.653
Barriers are sorted by when they act.

8
00:00:38.393 --> 00:00:43.693
Where the plants grow, and which pollinators visit them, act before the zygote, the

9
00:00:43.693 --> 00:00:49.453
fertilized egg. Low fertility in the hybrids acts after a hybrid zygote forms.

10
00:00:50.613 --> 00:00:54.353
One pair of species can be held apart by several barriers at once.

11
00:00:55.183 --> 00:00:57.463
Barriers act in sequence.

12
00:00:58.303 --> 00:01:02.643
Each one works only on the gene flow that the earlier barriers left behind.

13
00:01:03.903 --> 00:01:07.823
These numbers are illustrative, in the style of the monkeyflower study.

14
00:01:08.963 --> 00:01:13.763
Call the fraction of the remaining gene flow that a barrier blocks its RI.

15
00:01:14.403 --> 00:01:17.423
A barrier's credit is the gene flow it blocks.

16
00:01:18.523 --> 00:01:23.303
The first barrier, ecogeographic, has an RI of 0.60.

17
00:01:23.303 --> 00:01:28.823
It gets credit of 0.60, and 0.40 of the gene flow is left.

18
00:01:29.717 --> 00:01:37.597
The pollinator barrier has an RI of 0.90, but it acts only on the 0.40 that is left.

19
00:01:38.277 --> 00:01:47.877
It blocks 0.36. Then hybrid fertility, with an RI of 0.50 acts on the 0.04 that

20
00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:50.957
remains. It blocks 0.02.

21
00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.050
Total isolation is one minus what gets through.

22
00:01:57.190 --> 00:02:04.810
Multiply what each barrier lets through: 0.40 times 0.10 times 0.50.

23
00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:11.910
That is 0.02. So total isolation is 0.98.

24
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.150
Do not add the raw strengths.

25
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:19.590
They sum to 2.00, which means nothing as a fraction of gene flow.

26
00:02:20.483 --> 00:02:23.003
Now swap the first two barriers.

27
00:02:23.723 --> 00:02:28.263
The pollinator barrier acts first and gets 0.90 of the credit.

28
00:02:29.063 --> 00:02:32.763
The ecogeographic barrier gets only 0.06.

29
00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:36.783
Hybrid fertility still gets 0.02.

30
00:02:37.643 --> 00:02:39.903
The total is still 0.98.

31
00:02:41.063 --> 00:02:46.683
A barrier can only block the gene flow left for it, so credit depends on position as

32
00:02:46.683 --> 00:02:53.083
well as strength. Barriers act on what remains, so order moves the credit, not the total.
